<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="62513" href="schedule/2018/spring/GLBL/296/62513.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120181" href="schedule/2018/spring.xml">Spring 2018</term><subject id="GLBL" href="schedule/2018/spring/GLBL.xml">Global Studies</subject><course id="296" href="schedule/2018/spring/GLBL/296.xml">Global St Foundation Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>D  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Human Rights in the Midwest</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 16-Jan-18 - 09-Mar-18.</sectionDateRange><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course explores the concept of human rights and applies its principles to analyze social justice issues in the Midwestern United States. Topics covered include education, employment, housing, healthcare, and law enforcement. Students will use international conventions on human rights to examine circumstances in both rural and urban contexts. The course will highlight diverse experiences of human rights and different perspectives on what human rights are.</sectionText><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2018-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2018-03-09Z</endDate><specialApproval>Departmental Approval Required</specialApproval><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>06:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2078</roomNumber><buildingName>Natural History Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Goodnight" firstName="M">Goodnight, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>